    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="d387-01" n="1" xml:id="d387-01"/>

                <head>387. Letter From the Australian Ambassador (Plimsoll) to the President’s
                    Assistant for National Security Affairs (Kissinger)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d387-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d387-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1972-01-13"
                        >January 13, 1972</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Dear Dr Kissinger,</p>
                <p>I attach a message to the President which I have received from the Prime Minister
                    of Australia, about the situation on the Indian subcontinent, and I would be
                    grateful if you would pass it to the President. I am also passing a copy to the
                    Secretary of State.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>(V.Plimsoll)</signed>
                    <affiliation>Ambassador</affiliation></closer>


                <xi:include href="d387-a1.xml" xpointer="d387-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d387-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d387-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, NSC
                    Institutional Files (H-Files), Box H-062, SRG Meeting, South Asia, 1/19/72. Top
                    Secret</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d387-f2" n="2" xml:id="d387-f2-content">
                <p>Plimsoll forwarded a message from Australian Prime Minister McMahon to President
                    Nixon. McMahon pointed up his concern about Soviet influence in South Asia and
                    argued the importance of repairing relations with India and providing economic
                    assistance to the new nation of Bangladesh.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
